# AudioMixing

[中文](https://github.com/haop2922-ai/AudioMixing/blob/HEAD/README.md) | [English](https://github.com/haop2922-ai/AudioMixing/blob/HEAD/README.en.md)

> Let two people each wear their own headphones and play games / watch movies together.

Runs only on the local network, does not go through a server, and requires no account.

[⬇️ Download Windows version](https://github.com/haop2922-ai/AudioMixing/releases) · [⬇️ Download Android version](https://github.com/haop2922-ai/AudioMixing/releases)

✅ 584 unit tests · tests run automatically before building; no exe is produced if they fail

## How it differs from other audio forwarding software

Common audio forwarding software (such as AudioRelay) works as **one computer acting as a radio station, with other devices acting as radios**, a one-way star structure. AudioMixing's structure is **symmetric**:

- Every computer can be both a source of sound and a speaker for sound;
- The routing table is shared across the entire local network. Change it on any machine and it takes effect on all machines;
- Each route can be muted or have its volume adjusted independently;
- Sound coming in from a phone via Bluetooth can serve as an audio source and be forwarded to other rooms;
- One computer can send sound to multiple headphones / speakers at the same time (for two-player games);
- Broadcasting and "listen-only" are mutually exclusive: you either speak or listen, so a feedback loop cannot form structurally;
- There are two versions of phone-as-speaker: a web version (scan a QR code and use immediately, nothing to install) and an App version (native playback, lower latency).

## Not suitable for

- If you only want the single task of "computer sound to phone", dedicated software for that scenario is easier;
- Needing cross-network / relay: this project deliberately only does the local network;
- Needing macOS / Linux / iOS: currently only Windows + Android are supported;
- Needing "lossless, absolutely no stutter" professional audio transmission: ordinary Wi-Fi cannot achieve this, and this project does not provide an audio interface.

## Quick start

### Scenario 1: two computers sending audio to each other

```text
1. Run AudioMixing on both computers (exe or start.bat)
2. Right-click the tray icon → allow through the firewall (requires administrator) → click "Yes"
3. The browser automatically opens the console http://127.0.0.1:17800
4. On the one you want to listen on, create a route: from [the other computer] to [this computer]
```
